@startmindmap exp1_map
title Experiment 1 - map: is the measuring apparatus trustworthy?
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF

* Exp 1: sanity check
** Question
*** Before trusting any timing, does the apparatus do what it claims?
** Checks
*** Atomics and sizes
**** 64-byte cache line (from sysfs)
**** atomic uint64 is lock-free
**** counters are 8 bytes
*** Layouts from runtime addresses
**** Packed: 8 counters in one line
**** Padded: each counter in its own line
*** Topology
**** at least 8 distinct physical cores
*** NEGATIVE CONTROL
**** LoadStoreCounter on 2 threads MUST lose updates
**** proves the count check can actually fail
*** Every real contender is exact
**** fetch_add, CAS loop, spinlock, mutex
**** 2 threads and 8 threads on one counter
** Setup
*** 2 M increments per thread
*** CPUs 2 and 4 for 2 threads, first 8 physical cores for 8 threads
** Result
*** ALL CHECKS PASSED in 5 of 5 runs
*** Negative control lost 14.9 to 50.6 percent of increments
** Concepts to read first
*** Concept 01: the lost update
*** Concept 02: what atomic means
@endmindmap
